+
+## SMS sign-up verification
+
+Sign-up uses the same-origin `api/signup` endpoint. It sends and checks codes with
+Twilio Verify, then calls the existing registration service only after approval.
+Set these server environment variables (never `PUBLIC_` variables):
+
+- `TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID`
+- `TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN`
+- `TWILIO_VERIFY_SERVICE_SID`
+- `TWILIO_VERIFY_TEMPLATE_SID` (optional custom SMS template override)
+
+Configure the Verify service to issue **six-digit codes**. For automatic extraction,
+configure a [domain-bound SMS template](https://www.twilio.com/en-us/blog/developers/best-practices/otp-input-forms-html)
+on the service or supply its SID above. The SMS must end with a line such as
+`@your-deployed-host.example #123456`, using the actual host and the generated code.
+Use HTTPS. The form starts [WebOTP](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/web-apis/web-otp)
+listening before delivery; native `one-time-code` autofill and manual entry are also
+available. SMS extraction fills the field; the user explicitly submits it.
+
+Enable Twilio Verify Fraud Guard, geographic permissions and service rate limits
+before public deployment. The form also applies a 60-second resend delay; provider
+limits enforce attempts independently of the browser. Codes are checked at the
+provider and never generated or accepted locally. Missing credentials return an
+unavailable error rather than simulating delivery. No live SMS tests are run by the
+build.
+
+The external registration API remains responsible for account persistence and
+uniqueness. This app passes the verified phone as `phone`; that API must support
+storing it and restrict any direct registration paths if verification must be
+mandatory for all API clients. It is hosted outside this repository. If account
+creation fails after verification consumes a code, request a fresh code before
+retrying.
